<title>UK: Siebe mulls options as Whessoe bid trumped.</title>
<headline>Siebe mulls options as Whessoe bid trumped.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK electronic controls company Siebe said on Wednesday it was mulling its options after its bid for UK-based instruments and controls firm Whessoe Plc was trumped.</p>
<p>Two European technology firms, Norway's Seatex ASA and Swiss-based  Endress+Hauser earlier launched a 52.6 million stg bid for Whessoe, topping Siebe's 46 million pound agreed bid.</p>
<p>A Siebe spokesman said the company would make a formal response in due course.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
